        <div class="lg:order-1">
          <p class="mb-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-accent">XXV · Family and Personal Memory</p>
          <h2 class="mb-8 text-4xl font-heading font-bold leading-tight text-maintext md:text-5xl">
            Music also preserves the people closest to us
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-subtext">
            <p>
              Köksal has written personal compositions connected with both of his
              daughters, <strong class="text-maintext">Bernaz Su Köksal</strong> and
              <strong class="text-maintext">Arya Belinda Köksal</strong>. These works
              occupy a different place from the large public concepts: they preserve
              family feeling, memory and the relationship between a father and his
              children.
            </p>

            <p>
              His family life has also intersected directly with the sacred music
              journey, most clearly in Arya Belinda's childhood participation in a
              zikr recording and in the later children's-choir concept of
              <em>One God One Love</em>.
